{"change_summary":"No additional source edits were required in this apply-fixes pass. The current workspace already contains the approved explicit carbonate-equilibrium rollout and its later follow-up amendments, so this stage verified the integrated state rather than patching code again.","outstanding_risks":["`solve_carbonate_equilibrium()` still uses the freshwater-focused approximation with fixed `Ka2`, so any extension beyond the intended pH 5.5-8.5 aquarium envelope should revisit the chemistry model.","Legacy saves with custom out-of-range source-water catalog entries still deserialize, but runtime water-change actions against those profiles fail validation until the profile is corrected.","The unrelated untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory remains in the worktree and was left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Review the latest approved carbonate-equilibrium state and inspect the current workspace for unresolved tracked deltas or pending follow-up fixes.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Apply any remaining carbonate/save-path/snapshot follow-up edits; skipped because the workspace already contained the approved implementation and no new actionable review amendments remained.","order":1,"status":"skipped"},{"description":"Re-run workspace validation and code-path scans to confirm the approved implementation remains green in the current checkout.","order":2,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`git status --short` showed no tracked source deltas; only the unrelated untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory is present.","`cargo fmt --all --check` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core -p tank_data -p tank_scenarios` passed across the full tank_core, tank_data, and tank_scenarios suites.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -p tank_data -p tank_scenarios --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.","A code-path scan confirmed the current workspace still routes through `solve_carbonate_equilibrium()`, `normalize_loaded_carbonate_state()`, `validate_source_water_carbonate_profile()`, and `resolve_carbonate_state()`, and the old shortcut appears only in historical docs notes rather than runtime Rust code."]}